    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d992">

                <pb facs="0871" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/236.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1170.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexican Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 21, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In compliance with telegraphic
                    instructions received from my Government, I have the honor to apply for your
                    excellency’s good offices to obtain from the President of the United States of
                    America a declaration under the head of exceptions spoken of in his proclamation
                    of the 14th instant permitting the shipment to Mexico of the following arms and
                    ammunition intended for my Government: Three hundred carbines and 40,000
                    cartridges that are detained at Presidio, Texas; 15 cases with 150 rifles and 70
                    cases with 70,000 cartridges that are also detained at Shafter, Texas; and the
                    armament and park which the consul of Mexico at El Paso, Texas, forwarded to
                    General Sanjinés at Ojinaga, and which were detained by the authorities of this
                    Government at Marfa, Texas.</p>
                <p>I thank your excellency for such action as you may be pleased to take on this
                    request and beg [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilberto Crespo y Martínez.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
